[length:03:53.00]
[00:02.00]I say I trust Your holy Word, (8)
[00:09.90]Yet fear still fills my mind. (6)
[00:17.79]I ask You, Lord, to lead my steps, (8)
[00:25.69]Then leave Your way behind. (6)
[00:33.59]You said a mustard seed could move (8)
[00:41.48]The mountains from their place. (6)
[00:49.38]But often I depend upon (8)
[00:57.28]My effort, not Your grace. (6)
[01:05.17]I pray and lay my burdens down, (8)
[01:13.07]Then lift them up once more. (6)
[01:20.97]I claim the promises You gave, (8)
[01:28.86]Yet worry as before. (6)
[01:36.76]If I believe Your every word, (8)
[01:44.66]Why do I doubt and fear? (6)
[01:52.55]Why do I search for other plans (8)
[02:00.45]When You are always near? (6)
[02:08.34]Lord, teach my heart what faith can be, (8)
[02:16.24]To trust and then obey. (6)
[02:24.14]Not leaning on my strength alone, (8)
[02:32.03]But following Your way. (6)
[02:39.93]The mountain moves not by my might, (8)
[02:47.83]Nor by the faith I show. (6)
[02:55.72]It moves because the God I serve (8)
[03:03.62]Commands it where to go. (6)
[03:11.52]Final Chorus
[03:19.41]Lord, grow this tiny seed in me, (8)
[03:27.31]Though small it now may be. (6)
[03:35.21]For mustard-seed faith placed in You (8)
[03:43.10]Is all You'll ask of me. (6)
